MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

If you include a variable in regression equations, but the variable is not dependent on any other variable in the model, then it is a control variable (whether observed variable or common factor), then it is taken to be an exogenous control variable. The question is  whether or not the variable is subject to random sampling error. That is, is it "fixed" (so that the "fixed.x=TRUE" would be correct) or is it sampled (in which case the fixed.x specification would be incorrect)?

On Thu, Sep 6, 2018 at 12:56 AM <katja.si...@gmail.com> wrote:

> Hi!
>
