> it looks to me that all the model is fitting well.

Correct, the chi-squared test does not reject the null hypothesis of exact fit in the population.

> What indices should I report in a paper?

Chi-squared is enough, but most journals prefer reporting at least 2 other measures of fit (e.g., RMSEA, CFI, and/or SRMR are the most common).

https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1207/S15328007SEM0703_6

