> I would like NOT to use common itens in the measurements.Is this possible?

No, you need some linking items in order to link the scales of the latent traits across time.  Without overlapping items, you have no basis for linking scales.

> My understanding is that
>
> With Model 1, the scale of the items in moments 1 and 2 will be different. Is this correct?

Yes.

> With Model 2, the scale of the items in moments 1 and 2 will be the same. Is this correct?

No, but they can be put on the same scale by applying equality constraints to the loadings over time.

>
> With Model 3, the scale of the items in moments 1 and 2 will be the same. The assumption here is that the items will be equated with the linking test. Is this correct?

Only if you can constrain the loadings of the common items across time.

> If yes, how can  I pass these info to LAVAAN?

In lavaan's model syntax, you can apply the same label to multiple parameters.  Parameters with the same label will have the same estimated value.  For example, if items "x" measure Time 1 and items "y" measure Time 2, and items 1-3 are in common across time:

model <- '
    T1 =~ L1*x1 + L2*x2 + L3*x3 + x4 + x5
    T2 =~ L1*y1 + L2*y2 + L3*y3 + y6 + y7
'

